WEBVTT

welcome-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.769
Hi Gareth.

welcome-2
00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:04.231
This short video explains your mortgage offer from Fernmoor.

welcome-3
00:00:04.231 --> 00:00:06.154
It takes about two minutes.

welcome-4
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:11.154
You can pause, turn on captions, or ask a question at any time.

your-loan-1
00:00:11.154 --> 00:00:14.231
You're remortgaging your home, which is worth £420,000.

your-loan-2
00:00:14.231 --> 00:00:16.154
Your new loan is £210,999.

your-loan-3
00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:18.462
That's 50 percent of its value.

your-loan-4
00:00:18.462 --> 00:00:21.154
Lenders call this your loan to value.

your-loan-5
00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.846
You'll pay it back over 20 years.

your-rate-1
00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:28.462
For the first 5 years, your rate is fixed at 4.19 percent.

your-rate-2
00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:32.692
Your monthly payment stays at £1,299.84, even if interest rates change.

after-fixed-1
00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:35.769
Your fixed rate ends on 31 October 2031.

after-fixed-2
00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.231
After that, you move to our Standard Variable Rate.

after-fixed-3
00:00:39.231 --> 00:00:43.462
It's 7.49 percent today, and it can go up or down.

after-fixed-4
00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:48.462
If it stays the same, your payment would rise to £1,607.25 a month.

after-fixed-5
00:00:48.462 --> 00:00:49.615
That's £307.41 more.

after-fixed-6
00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:53.846
Many people choose a new deal before their fixed rate ends.

overpayments-1
00:00:53.846 --> 00:01:00.769
You can pay off up to 10 percent of what you owe each year at no extra cost.

overpayments-2
00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:06.538
If you repay more than that during your fixed rate, there's an early repayment charge.

overpayments-3
00:01:06.538 --> 00:01:12.692
It starts at 5 percent in year 1 and falls to 1 percent in year 5.

overpayments-4
00:01:12.692 --> 00:01:18.077
For example, repaying an extra ten thousand pounds in year 1 would cost £500.

fees-1
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.385
There's a product fee of £999.00.

fees-2
00:01:20.385 --> 00:01:23.462
You chose to add it to your loan.

fees-3
00:01:23.462 --> 00:01:28.846
That means you don't pay it upfront, but you will pay interest on it.

total-cost-1
00:01:28.846 --> 00:01:34.615
Over the full 20 years, you'd repay about £367,295 in total, if rates don't change.

total-cost-2
00:01:34.615 --> 00:01:38.846
That includes your loan of £210,999 and the interest on it.

your-part-1
00:01:38.846 --> 00:01:42.308
There are a few things you need to do.

your-part-2
00:01:42.308 --> 00:01:43.846
Keep up your payments.

your-part-3
00:01:43.846 --> 00:01:46.923
Your home may be repossessed if you don't.

your-part-4
00:01:46.923 --> 00:01:48.462
Keep your home insured.

your-part-5
00:01:48.462 --> 00:01:52.308
And remember, this offer is valid until 22 March 2027.

contact-1
00:01:52.308 --> 00:01:57.692
If anything isn't clear, type a question in the box next to this video.

contact-2
00:01:57.692 --> 00:02:01.538
Or call us on 01632 960412 and quote your reference.

contact-3
00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:03.077
Thanks for watching, Gareth.
